{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788137012,"nonce":"ts6CDdkhuRkTu7Svi6GoudWYyM4=","message":"CLOSED — acceptance verified personally by the orchestrator on the BORGES\nbench, session 5. Merged to main fast-forward (cf8e68f..5ea7034 + Build\nf15f69e). All commands ran through the real file protocol (no python on this\nbox, so raw JSON command files stood in for rwa); bench session\nsid 20260831T001913, quicktest colony, dev mode on.\n\n\nTwo independent readers per number, per the stockpile-step discipline: the\n`pawn-fixture` steps hand back expectations computed directly from the game\nmodel at mutation time, and the save file gives the Scribe path. The\nserializer had to agree with both.\n\n- **Registration**: unknown-op listed `pawn`, `pawn-fixture`, `pawns` among 19\n  ops on first boot.\n- **Fixture** (`wound`+`sadden`+`tatter` on the first standing colonist,\n  Gibbs id 221): wounded AND standing (8 injuries, downed:false, bleed 1.83,\n  summary 68%), 4 DebugBad + 1 DebugGood memories, both apparel items set to\n  20/130 HP.\n- **Mood %**: `mood.pct` 56 == fixture's 56; `instant_pct` 37 == 37; arrow −1\n  consistent.\n- **Top thought offsets**: all six fixture-expected groups present at\n  identical offsets (Expectations +24, DebugGood +10, NewColonyOptimism +10,\n  Pain_Idealized +5, EnvironmentCold −4, DebugBad −40 count:4), order strictly\n  monotone descending — PLUS `ApparelDamaged −5`, which appeared because the\n  tatter step ran after sadden computed its expectations: the wear→mood chain\n  observed live, end to end.\n- **Hediff list**: 9/9 exact against BOTH readers — the fixture's direct\n  hediffSet read and the save XML (6 Cut + 2 Crack at 3.27/4.24 severities +\n  the pawn's pre-existing HandTalon implant). A tenth hediff in my first save\n  extraction turned out to belong to the next animal in the file — checked and\n  excluded, not waved through. Urgency-desc ordering held (bleeding first).\n- **Apparel HP%**: 20/130 → hp_pct 15, wear \"tattered\" on both items,\n  matching the fixture's expect_wear and the save's `\u003chealth\u003e20\u003c/health\u003e`;\n  `worst_wear:\"tattered\"`; the game's own Tattered-apparel alert appeared at\n  the same tick.\n- **Skill levels**: 12/12 exact against the save XML's scribed levels and\n  passions. The `level` vs `level_raw` divergence shipped correct and was\n  observed live: Intellectual prints 0 (permanently disabled, \"coma child\"\n  backstory) while level_raw is the stored 3 — and `work.disabled` names\n  DarkStudy/Research consistently.\n- **`use_priorities:false`** published on a fresh quicktest colony (manual\n  priorities off), exactly the flat-3 trap disclosure the catalogue demanded.\n- **Prisoner**: fixture capture through the game's own\n  `SetGuestStatus(Prisoner)` path. `class:\"prisoner\"`,\n  `guest.status:\"Prisoner\"`, `host_faction:\"PlayerColony\"`, resistance 15 /\n  will 0.34 — both matching the fixture's rolled expectations, both real\n  numbers rather than the −1 sentinel. **The lazy-init-write guard proved\n  itself live**: `policies` came back `{apparel:null, food:null, drug:null,\n  source:\"backing-field\"}` — a fresh prisoner genuinely has no policies, and\n  the raw getters would have permanently assigned and scribed them. The\n  prisoner then escaped (no cell — the ThreatSmall letter three ticks later is\n  the escape announcement) and walked off-map over the next hours; correct\n  game behaviour, noted so the next reader is not surprised.\n- **Error paths**: unknown filter and unknown section each return bad-args\n  naming the full legal set; an absent id returns the policy-naming denial\n  that does not confirm the pawn exists.\n- **Caps + by_class**: 45 animals at cap 5 → 5 listed, more:40; by_class\n  complete on every call; attention order with id tie-break visible in the\n  roster.\n- **Opinions**: off by default with the disclosure note in the payload; opt-in\n  queried 1 of pool 1 (only two colonists left by then), best/worst populated.\n- **Zero red errors** across the entire exercise — the session journal holds\n  no red_error events at all, Player.log 0 exceptions, boot warnings the\n  known-benign set.\n\n\n- **Visitor**: NOT demonstrated live. The `visitor` fixture step fired\n  (`TryExecute` returned true), but on this bench **the Factions director owns\n  visitor arrivals** — Player.log: \"Hospitality visitor-queue fill skipped —\n  the director owns the supply\", \"a group the director sent spawns inside its\n  window\" — and no visitor or guest spawned across 2+ in-game days of\n  advancing on a collapsing colony. The visitor/guest branches of the\n  classification ladder are code-reviewed only; the ladder itself was\n  demonstrated live for colonist / animal / wildlife / prisoner. This is also\n  M3-relevant bench knowledge: forced vanilla VisitorGroup incidents are\n  swallowed by the director on this modlist, so Factions/Guests suites must\n  drive arrivals through the director's own machinery, not the incident.\n- **Fog hiding**: the quicktest map had no fogged pawn to hide (open terrain,\n  skipped.fogged_or_unspawned stayed 0), so the skip was not observed live;\n  one shared `Hidden()` route on both verbs plus the non-confirming denial is\n  code-reviewed.\n- **\"Matches the in-game inspect values\"** was verified against the game's own\n  model numbers through two independent read paths (fixture-time direct reads;\n  save-file Scribe XML), with the decompile-verified print paths\n  (CalculateCapacityLevel, GetLevelForUI, ThoughtWorker_ApparelDamaged\n  thresholds) as the bridge to what the tabs draw — not by reading the\n  rendered UI pixel-for-pixel.\n\n\n- Full 13-section drill-down on a wounded pawn measured **~8.7KB**, not the\n  ~4KB the worker estimated; a 2-section subset (needs+mood) is 1.9KB.\n  Sections are the economy lever and the spec set no drill-down budget, so\n  this is flagged, not failed — but 4.2 should ask for sections, not the\n  firehose.\n- Manhunters classify as wildlife, not hostile (the animal test precedes the\n  hostile test in the ladder); their mental state rides in `flags`. Documented\n  consequence, defensible, noted for 3.4.\n- JOURNAL.md's dev-row now names pawn-fixture as the second dev-event writer\n  (orchestrator commit on main).","files":null}]}